# --- Original media, firmware, and third-party SDK archives: never committed ---
# Apple ROMs, Berkeley Systems' modules and SDKs, and disk images are someone
# else's copyrighted material. The whole folder is a local-only cache so they
# don't have to be re-downloaded or re-extracted — see "Getting the original
# assets" in docs/technical-notes.md for how to reconstitute it.
/reference/
*.ROM
Old_World_Mac_Roms.zip
New_World_Mac_Roms.zip

# The source disk image and anything extracted from it.
AfterDark-original.img
*.img
!fixtures/**/*.img

# Extracted original assets and generated module packs. No exceptions, and no
# whitelist below this line: the modules and fonts are Berkeley Systems' and
# Apple's, and the app imports them from the user's own disk at first launch
# rather than carrying them.
/modules/
**/forks/
*.rsrc

# Oracle captures (large, regenerable; commit hashes not frames).
/tests/oracle/captures/

# --- Build output ---
# dist/ is where make_app.sh and make_dist.sh leave their output locally. The
# published downloads are GitHub Release assets, built by
# .github/workflows/release.yml on a version tag — a binary is a pure function
# of the commit it came from, so it does not belong in history.
/dist/
/target/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# --- Scratch ---
*.pyc
__pycache__/

trapscan.json
repomix-output.xml

# Disc images: Berkeley Systems' software, not this project's.
*.iso
*.iso.zip
